  "summary": "Patient presents with a one-week history of painless, mildly warm swelling of the left elbow noted incidentally, without trauma. History of osteoarthritis and a peanut allergy. Examination showed mild erythema and swelling around the olecranon with no signs of an acutely infected joint. Diagnosed as probable olecranon bursitis. Advised anti-inflammatory medication, blood tests to exclude other causes of joint swelling, and a follow-up review, with safety-netting for signs of septic arthritis."
